<div dir=3D"auto">Dear Robert Samuel White:<br>
<br>
Thank you for your interest in public records of Oregon Department of Trans=
portation. Your request has been received and is being processed in accorda=
nce with the ORS 192.311 - 478, Oregon Public Records Law.&nbsp; Your reque=
st was received in this office on 9/5/2026
 and given the reference number R027904-090526 for tracking purposes.<br>
<br>
<b>Records Requested:</b> This is a request under the Oregon Public Records=
 Law. It is narrow and concerns one individual.<br>
<br>
Lisa Sumption served as interim director of the Oregon Department of Transp=
ortation from January 2, 2026 until approximately the end of June 2026, whi=
le continuing to hold the position of director of the Oregon Parks and Recr=
eation Department. This request
 concerns records held by the Department of Transportation relating to me d=
uring and after that period.<br>
<br>
I am Robert Samuel White, date of birth April 11, 1977. I was an unpaid vol=
unteer with the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department and was permanently =
excluded from all Department volunteer programs in a letter dated March 26,=
 2025. I have corresponded with
 Director Sumption about that matter since August 2025. On March 24, 2026 =
=97 during her ODOT tenure =97 Oregon State Police detectives and a federal=
 officer came to my residence following a referral made by an OPRD employee=
.<br>
<br>
The period requested is January 1, 2026 to the present.<br>
<br>
I request the following.<br>
<br>
1. All records concerning me held by the Oregon Department of Transportatio=
n, in any division or function, including records indexed under Robert Whit=
e, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White, Sam White, rsw@rswfire.com, oprdvo=
lunteerabuse.org, rswfire.com, or
 my date of birth.<br>
<br>
2. All communications concerning me sent or received by Lisa Sumption using=
 any Oregon Department of Transportation email account, device, or system, =
in any medium, including email, text message, instant message, and any mess=
aging application.<br>
<br>
3. All records concerning me created, received, or held by any other Depart=
ment of Transportation employee.<br>
<br>
4. All communications between the Department of Transportation and the Oreg=
on Parks and Recreation Department, Oregon State Police, the Office of the =
Governor, the Department of Administrative Services, or the Department of J=
ustice concerning me.<br>
<br>
5. Any record reflecting the forwarding, transfer, deletion, or migration o=
f records concerning me between Department of Transportation systems and an=
y other agency's systems, including at the conclusion of Director Sumption'=
s interim appointment.<br>
<br>
6. Any record reflecting the retention or disposition of Lisa Sumption's De=
partment of Transportation email account and its contents following the end=
 of her interim appointment.<br>
<br>
For the purpose of this request, &quot;concerning me&quot; includes any rec=
ord referring to Robert White, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White, Sam Wh=
ite, my correspondence, my volunteer service with OPRD, my dismissal or exc=
lusion, my public records requests, the archive
 at oprdvolunteerabuse.org, the March 24, 2026 law enforcement contact at m=
y residence, or the legal fund I have opened.<br>
<br>
<br>
Administration<br>
<br>
Fee waiver. I request a waiver under ORS 192.324(5). Disclosure primarily b=
enefits the general public. These records concern whether a state agency di=
rector, while serving simultaneously at two agencies, used the systems of o=
ne to conduct business concerning
 a citizen's complaint against the other. I have no commercial purpose. All=
 records produced will be published in full, at no charge, at oprdvolunteer=
abuse.org.<br>
<br>
Acknowledgment and timeline. ORS 192.324(2) requires acknowledgment or comp=
letion within five business days, and ORS 192.329(5) requires a reasonable =
estimated completion date where a response cannot be completed within fifte=
en business days. I request both
 in writing.<br>
<br>
Fees. ORS 192.324(4) prohibits a fee exceeding $25 without prior written no=
tice. If a fee is to be charged, I request that notice with an itemized bas=
is before any work is performed, and the opportunity to narrow the request =
rather than have it held pending
 payment. I have no ability to receive or return printed forms; any fee wai=
ver determination should not be conditioned on the return of a printed docu=
ment.<br>
<br>
Format. Electronic delivery by email or secure link, in native format with =
headers, recipients, timestamps, metadata, and attachments preserved and in=
tact.<br>
<br>
Preservation. Please treat all records responsive to this request as subjec=
t to litigation hold. I have served a notice of tort claim on the State of =
Oregon under ORS 30.275, and the Department of Administrative Services has =
opened claim P195403. This preservation
 request extends to any archived, backed-up, or deprovisioned account or ma=
ilbox associated with Lisa Sumption's interim appointment.<br>
<br>
Disposition. For each numbered item, please state whether responsive record=
s exist, produce them, or cite the specific exemption claimed for each reco=
rd or portion withheld, as ORS 192.329(2) requires. If the Department is no=
t the custodian of a category, please
 identify the custodian rather than closing the request as to that category=
. ORS 192.311(2)(b).<br>
<br>
Robert Samuel White<br>
oprdvolunteerabuse.org<br>
<br>
Your request will be forwarded to the relevant department(s) to locate the =
information you seek and to determine the volume and any costs associated w=
ith satisfying your request. You will be contacted about the availability a=
nd/or provided with copies of the
 records in question. PLEASE NOTE: Oregon Public Records Law&nbsp;does not =
require a governmental body to create new information, to do legal research=
, or to answer questions.<br>
<br>
You can monitor the progress of your request at the link below and you'll r=
eceive an email when your request has been completed. Again, thank you for =
using the Public Records Center.<br>
<br>
Oregon Department of Transportation</div>
